course: dictionary
lesson: 14634
title: Powerless
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Powerless is built from two parts: power and less. The ending -less means without, so powerless means without power. A powerless person or thing cannot do something, or cannot help.
explain: «The little boat was powerless against the huge waves.» The boat could not stop the waves or steer away from them. The clues are huge waves and little boat, so powerless must mean unable to fight back.
explain: Powerless can describe a feeling too. «Ben felt powerless when he could not help his friend.» Ben wanted to help but could not, so he felt unable to act. Ask yourself: what is missing here? The answer tells you the meaning.
fact: Powerless means without power or strength to do something.
fact: Powerless also means unable to help or act.
fact: The ending -less means without, so careless means without care and hopeless means without hope.
fact: «Without batteries, the torch is powerless.» This means the torch cannot give out light.
fact: In history, people who had no vote were powerless to choose their leaders.
exercise: «The boat was powerless against the huge waves.» What does powerless mean here? | Very fast | *Unable to stop the waves | Painted bright red | Full of fish
exercise: «Without batteries, the torch is powerless.» Why is the torch powerless? | *It has no power to give out light | It is the wrong colour | It has been left in the sun | It is too heavy to lift
exercise: Ella says, «I felt powerless when the lift got stuck.» What does powerless suggest? | Hungry for lunch | *Unable to get out or change what was happening | Happy to be alone | Excited and eager to jump
test: «Ben felt powerless when he could not help his friend.» What does powerless suggest? | Very tired from running | Happy and proud | Angry and loud | *Unable to help
test: Look at the word parts: power plus less. What does powerless mean? | Very strong | Full of power | *Without power | Power to fly
exam: In history, people without a vote were powerless. What does powerless mean here? | Able to choose the leaders | Rich and famous | Very loud and angry | *Without the power to choose or change things
